# Template. Copy to .env and fill in. .env is git-ignored; this file is not.
#
# NOTHING IN THE PAPER NEEDS A CREDENTIAL.
# The forecasting experiment is closed and its results are the committed
# timeGPT_*.csv and chronos_*.csv. Both of these regenerate every published
# figure and table with no key set at all:
#
#     python -m superarc.parity
#     python -m superarc.cli --out outputs/<version>
#
# A key is needed only to RE-RUN the forecasts, which is not part of
# reproducing the paper.

# Nixtla TimeGPT-1 -- https://dashboard.nixtla.io
# Read by superarc.credentials.nixtla_api_key().
NIXTLA_API_KEY=

# Never put a key in a .py or .ipynb file. Two were put into
# processing_answers.py, and they are still readable in this repository's public
# git history and in AlgoDynLab/SuperintelligenceTest. Deleting a secret from the
# working tree does not unpublish it -- it has to be revoked.
